WASTEPAY - TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE


1. PURPOSE

The WastePay Technical Architecture defines the full-stack infrastructure, security model, deployment strategy, and system design principles required to operate a scalable circular economy platform across Africa.



--------------------------------------------------


2. ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLES

WastePay is designed using the following principles:

- Serverless First
- Mobile First
- Offline First
- Security First
- Financial Immutability
- Environmental Intelligence by Design
- Geographic Intelligence by Design
- Public Transparency by Design
- Multi-Country Scalability
- Role-Based Access Control



--------------------------------------------------


3. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE LAYERS

Presentation Layer

- Public Website
- Progressive Web Application
- Admin Dashboard


Application Layer

- Next.js 15+
- App Router
- React Server Components
- Server Actions


Business Logic Layer

- Pricing Engine
- Payment Engine
- Logistics Engine
- Barcode Intelligence Engine
- Collection Engine


Data Layer

- PostgreSQL
- Supabase
- PostGIS
- Supabase Storage


Infrastructure Layer

- Vercel
- Mobile Money APIs
- Mapping Services
- Notification Services



--------------------------------------------------


4. SERVERLESS INFRASTRUCTURE

Deployment Platform:

- Vercel

Framework:

- Next.js 15+
- TypeScript

Routing Strategy:

Public Website:

- Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR)

Private Applications:

- Server Side Rendering (SSR)



--------------------------------------------------


5. AUTHENTICATION ARCHITECTURE

Authentication Requirements:

- JWT based authentication.
- Role-based authorization.
- Type-safe session management.

User roles are mapped directly to:

- Supabase profiles table.



--------------------------------------------------


6. ROW LEVEL SECURITY POLICIES

Collectors:

- Read only their own transactions.

Depot Agents:

- Insert operational records.
- Read operational records.

Depot Managers:

- Manage transactions within assigned depots.

Super Administrators:

- Full administrative access.

Business Rule:

All financial and operational access is protected by Supabase RLS policies.



--------------------------------------------------


7. MOBILE EXECUTION LAYER

Barcode Scanning:

- html5-qrcode

Image Processing:

- Browser-side image compression.

Photo Upload Pipeline:

- Maximum compressed size under 500 KB.

Location Services:

- Browser Geolocation API.

Spatial Data:

- PostGIS geography types using SRID 4326.



--------------------------------------------------


8. STORAGE ARCHITECTURE

Supabase Storage Buckets include:

- collector-verifications
- pickup-photos
- barcode-products
- depot-images
- campaign-assets
- public-impact-assets



--------------------------------------------------


9. PAYMENT ARCHITECTURE

Supported Providers:

- MTN Mobile Money
- Orange Money

Payment Processing:

- Next.js Server Actions
- Secure server-side execution.

Business Rule:

Payment credentials are never exposed to client applications.



--------------------------------------------------


10. ASYNCHRONOUS PAYMENT WORKERS

Supports:

- Payment retries.
- Telecom polling.
- Status reconciliation.
- Exponential backoff strategies.
- Offline payment recovery.



--------------------------------------------------


11. GEOGRAPHIC INTELLIGENCE LAYER

Powered by:

- PostgreSQL
- PostGIS

Supports:

- Depot service zones.
- Collection requests.
- Driver tracking.
- Route optimization.
- Geographic analytics.



--------------------------------------------------


